; The classic unstratifiable program — `p ← absent q; q ← absent p`.
;
; Both guards pass against the empty world, so a boundary that admitted a
; whole round's worth of candidates would derive **both** — and `{p, q}` is
; not a model of this program under any reading. S1.21.8 admits **at most one
; candidate per round** for exactly this reason: the queue is empty at
; quiescence, so the admitted candidate fires immediately, against exactly the
; world its guard was judged against, and the other candidate is re-judged
; against the world that firing made.
;
; What this fixture pins is therefore not *which* of the two is derived — that
; is the engine's own (priority, FIFO) order and it is deterministic — but that
; exactly one is, and that the second candidate is then **retired** rather than
; left waiting: its guard is monotone, so once it finds a match it finds one
; forever.
;
; The one-at-a-time discipline is a soundness requirement, not a throttle, and
; the argument for it is a fixture rather than a comment.
;
; ── 2026-11-04 — what the search answers: M1e2 W8, deferred to F21 ─────────
;
; Saturation derives `(p one)` alone. The search then commits the one
; candidate, `(q one)`, in a node built by fork from root, so that node holds
; `(p one)`, derived under `(absent (q one))`, beside `(q one)`: the `{p, q}`
; above. Re-taken at M1e2 S1e2.2.6 (2026-11-04; `ein solve` in each mode and
; `ein oracle`, every one exiting 0): R is two states, ∅ (root) and
; `{(q one)}` (the fork, holding both). `--maximal` prints `(q one)`,
; `--minimal` ∅, `--single` `Ambiguity`, and the oracle the same R. Every
; read-out carries P1e2.1b's detector: not monotone, two `absent` sites in an
; even cycle, and the stale fact, `(p one) ← derive-p (absent (q one))`, in R.
;
; Whether that is wrong is Q-M1e2.2, what a node holds when a guard's witness
; arrives in its commitment: register row `W8/features-07`
; (`corpus/wrong_answers.toml`), contested. Under *guards are premises* the
; maximal state is `{(q one)}` alone; under *refuse what cannot be stratified*
; this file is a load error; under *append-only* today's R stands. The user
; deferred the reading to F21's D2 and amended M1e2's acceptance on
; 2026-11-03 (*"(2) Amend acceptance"*): the row stays `open`, reviewed
; `deferred`, owner F21, and the milestone closes naming it. *Forbid* (M1e2
; S1e2.2.5), which refuses `stale-naf-fork.ein`, does not reach this file:
; both rules conclude a positive fact, so nothing here refutes. No `:expect`
; is stated, so `ein test` has nothing to check.
(relation thing Thing :why "{?1} is a thing")
(relation p Thing :why "{?1} is p")
(relation q Thing :why "{?1} is q")

(rule derive-p ()
  :match  (and (thing ?x) (absent (q ?x)))
  :assert (p ?x)
  :why    "no q for {?x}, so p")

(rule derive-q ()
  :match  (and (thing ?x) (absent (p ?x)))
  :assert (q ?x)
  :why    "no p for {?x}, so q")

(thing one :source "the only object")
